    "diagramPlacement": "right-of-prompt",
    "answer": {
      "short": "Y has twice the base of X but the same height, so the triangles are not similar.",
      "worked": "X has base $2$ grid units and height $4$ grid units. Y has base $4$ grid units and height $4$ grid units.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Base ratio}&=\\frac{4}{2}=2\\\\\\text{Height ratio}&=\\frac{4}{4}=1\\end{align*}$$\nThe ratios differ, so Y is not a uniform enlargement of X.",
